[38;5;231m⏺[39m Classification first: [1marchitectural[0m. This repo is a single static [38;5;153mindex.html[39m with an empty [38;5;153m<main>[39m — there is no task
  model, no user model, no server, no storage. "Notify users when tasks they care about change" presupposes all four. So
  this isn't a bounded change to an existing flow; it's new structure, and it gets the full treatment: questions →
  approaches → design → spec → plan. No code until you approve a design.

  One scope flag before I start refining details. As stated, this request contains at least four independent subsystems:

  1. [1mTasks[0m — a data model with a change history (nothing to notify about otherwise)
  2. [1mUsers + identity[0m — who "cares about" something, and who a notification is addressed to
  3. [1mSubscription/interest[0m — how a user comes to care about a task (assignee? watcher? project member?)
  4. [1mDelivery[0m — in-app feed, email, push, digest; each has different infrastructure

  Only #3 and #4 are really "the notifications system." #1 and #2 are prerequisites that don't exist yet. I don't want
  to spend clarifying questions on digest cadence if the real answer is that we're building a task app from scratch and
  notifications are phase three.

